/* Beat 7 - the payoff, composed onto ScreenScaffold. The hybrid is the warm
 * thing on a recessive ground (bible 10.1), so this is the one screen that
 * centres and enlarges.
 *
 * SIX RULES' WORTH OF TREATMENT LEFT THIS FILE IN PHASE 8 TASK 10 AND NONE
 * WAS REPLACED BY A COPY HERE:
 *   - the root's `padding: var(--gutter)` is the scaffold's content region.
 *   - `__headline`'s font-size, colour and weight are Theme's `.t-hero`,
 *     which is the same 28px this file was restating.
 *   - `__child-line`'s and `__consumption`'s colour and size are
 *     `.t-secondary`. The child line moves 12px -> 11px in the process,
 *     which is deliberate rather than incidental: it is a muted supporting
 *     sentence sitting under the hero card, exactly what the consumption
 *     line below it already is, and the two had no reason to be different
 *     sizes. 11px is bible 10.6's floor, not below it.
 *   - `__next`'s top margin is the CTA row's own padding and its width is
 *     what a column CTA row already stretches its children to; the button's
 *     whole treatment is Theme's `.btn-primary`.
 *
 * THE HERO WRAPPER IS `.elev-2 .reveal-flare` IN THE UXML, not rules here.
 * Both are existing vocabulary and this screen is the consumer each was
 * written for - Theme.uss's raised elevation is the heavier of the handoff's
 * two drops, and Motion.uss's reveal transition is one of the four classes
 * that file lists as "matching nothing today". A rule in THIS file would be
 * a third copy of a treatment that already has one place to live.
 */
.splice-reveal-view { flex-grow: 1; }

/* THE CENTRING IS ON THE SCAFFOLD'S CONTENT CONTAINER, which is the element
 * that actually holds these children - the ScrollView routes them into
 * `unity-scroll-view__content-container`, so `align-items` on any ancestor
 * above it does nothing. Reaching a descendant from a screen's own sheet is
 * the legal direction (CampaignSelectView.uss's note): a COMPONENT's sheet
 * cannot style the container it was put in, which is upward. */
.splice-reveal-view .unity-scroll-view__content-container { align-items: center; }

/* A mutation is the rare outcome and the reason the screen exists. Violet is
 * the brand colour and this is where it earns the emphasis. Two classes, so
 * it outranks `.t-hero`'s --ink. */
.splice-reveal-view.mutated .splice-reveal-view__headline { color: var(--violet-text); }

.splice-reveal-view__headline { white-space: normal; margin-bottom: var(--space-3); }

.splice-reveal-view__child { margin-bottom: var(--space-3); }

.splice-reveal-view__child-line { white-space: normal; margin-bottom: var(--space-1); }

/* The two consumed parents, still whole. bible 2.1 makes this the FTUE's
 * whole lesson, so they are shown at full strength and the consumption line
 * below carries the fact instead of the parents being greyed out. */
.splice-reveal-view__parents { flex-direction: row; justify-content: center; margin-top: var(--space-3); }

.splice-reveal-view__parent { margin-left: var(--space-1); margin-right: var(--space-1); }

.splice-reveal-view__consumption { white-space: normal; margin-top: var(--space-3); }
